Steven Piano — Android player for the self-playing acoustic piano
==================================================================

Original author, designer, and creator
--------------------------------------
Steven Jin  <stevenjin20090101@gmail.com>
  - The app: MIDI file engine, Bluetooth LE MIDI link, playback, library
    and import, and the interface
  - The self-playing piano it plays (firmware, system integration and the
    physical installation), in the sibling firmware project

Music library
-------------
The MIDI files the app plays are not part of this repository. The library
it was built for draws on MAESTRO (Google Magenta, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0),
piano-midi.de (Bernd Krüger, CC BY-SA) and the Mutopia Project (public
domain); their licences govern those files.

Third-party
-----------
Bravura music font (app/src/main/res/font/bravura.otf, version 1.482,
bundled unmodified), which draws the score's clefs, key and time
signatures, accidentals, note heads, flags, dots, rests, dynamics and the
tempo mark's note:
  Copyright © 2026, Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH
  (http://www.steinberg.net/), with Reserved Font Name "Bravura".
  Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1; the full licence
  is in third_party/bravura/OFL.txt and at https://openfontlicense.org.
  The font keeps its own licence; the MIT licence of this project does not
  apply to it.

Haze (dev.chrisbanes.haze:haze 1.7.2, linked unmodified from Maven
Central), which blurs the content beneath the glass of the floating
controls:
  Copyright 2023, Christopher Banes and the Haze project contributors.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). The library keeps its own
  licence; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to it.

NanoHTTPD (org.nanohttpd:nanohttpd and nanohttpd-websocket 2.3.1, linked
unmodified from Maven Central), the small HTTP and WebSocket server the web
panel runs on:
  Copyright (c) 2012 - 2016, nanohttpd.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License; the full licence, with its
  disclaimer, is in third_party/nanohttpd/LICENSE.txt. The names of
  nanohttpd and its contributors do not endorse this project. The library
  keeps its own licence; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to
  it.

qrcode-kotlin (io.github.g0dkar:qrcode-kotlin 4.5.0, its Android variant
qrcode-kotlin-android, linked unmodified from Maven Central), whose encoder
makes the QR codes of the panel's address and the request poster:
  Copyright (c) 2021 Rafael Lins.
  Licensed under the MIT License; the full licence is in
  third_party/qrcode-kotlin/LICENSE.txt. The library keeps its own licence.

EdDSA-Java (net.i2p.crypto:eddsa 0.3.0, linked unmodified from Maven
Central), which checks the Ed25519 signature of the piano's firmware
releases where Android has no Ed25519 of its own:
  By str4d and the EdDSA-Java contributors (https://github.com/str4d/ed25519-java).
  Dedicated to the public domain under Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal;
  the legal code is in third_party/eddsa/LICENSE.txt and at
  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/. The library keeps its
  own terms; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to it.

ONNX Runtime (com.microsoft.onnxruntime:onnxruntime-android 1.28.0, linked
unmodified from Maven Central), which runs Studio's models on the tablet:
  Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
  Licensed under the MIT License; the full licence is in
  third_party/onnxruntime/LICENSE.txt, and the notices of the third-party
  code it carries in third_party/onnxruntime/ThirdPartyNotices.txt. The
  library keeps its own licence.

Piano transcription model (Studio's transcription model; downloaded by the
app on demand, never bundled): "High-resolution Piano Transcription with
Pedals by Regressing Onsets and Offsets Times", trained model by Qiuqiang
Kong, Bochen Li, Xuchen Song, Yuan Wan and Yuxuan Wang (ByteDance),
https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4034264.
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
  (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Converted to
  ONNX and partly quantised to INT8 for Steven Piano (tools/studio/; what
  changed is in third_party/piano-transcription/NOTICE.txt). The model keeps
  its own licence; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to it.

Composing model (Studio's composing model; downloaded by the app on demand,
never bundled): the Anticipatory Music Transformer music-small-800k by John
Thickstun, David Hall, Chris Donahue and Percy Liang (Stanford CRFM),
https://huggingface.co/stanford-crfm/music-small-800k.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the full licence is in
  third_party/anticipatory-music-transformer/LICENSE.txt and at
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0. Exported to ONNX with a KV
  cache and quantised to INT8 for Steven Piano (tools/studio/; what changed
  is in third_party/anticipatory-music-transformer/NOTICE.txt). The model
  keeps its own licence; the MIT licence of this project does not apply to
  it.

Wikipedia text (fetched while the app runs, never bundled): composers'
blurbs and pieces' notes are text from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia,
by its contributors:
  Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
  International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The app shows each
  text with the line "Text from Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0" and a
  "From Wikipedia" link to the article it came from; it shortens blurbs to
  their first two sentences and changes nothing else. Portraits come from
  Wikimedia Commons, each under the licence its file page states. Neither
  the text nor the portraits are covered by this project's MIT licence.

